PatchClosure-Bench repro -- typo3-cve-2013-4321  (CVE-2013-4250 -> CVE-2013-4321)
Real Docker gate run 2026-07-11.  Variant A (same sink, same flag channel).

MECHANISM (source-verified, TYPO3 CMS File Abstraction Layer)
  Root cause: authenticated backend editor executes arbitrary PHP by renaming a file to a
  denied extension. The extension guard is GeneralUtility::verifyFilenameAgainstDenyPattern
  (regex FILE_DENY_PATTERN_DEFAULT = '\.(php[3-6]?|phpsh|phtml)(\..*)?$|^\.htaccess$', plus a
  [[:cntrl:]] control-char reject), wrapped by ResourceStorage::checkFileExtensionPermission,
  called from ResourceStorage::renameFile. The on-disk name is produced by
  LocalDriver::sanitizeFileName, whose FIRST step is trim($fileName).

  V0 TYPO3 6.0.4  -> renameFile() performs NO extension check                (pre CVE-2013-4250)
  V1 TYPO3 6.0.8  -> CVE-2013-4250 (SA-2013-002) adds the check on the RAW target name
  V2 TYPO3 6.0.9  -> CVE-2013-4321 (SA-2013-003) sanitises (trims) BEFORE checking

  RESIDUAL (CVE-2013-4321): "residual_shell.php " (one TRAILING SPACE) is not a control char and
  is not matched by the anchored regex ($ sits after the space), so it PASSES the RAW check on V1.
  sanitizeFileName then trim()s the space, so the file lands as "residual_shell.php" and Apache
  executes it. V2 trims before checking, so the name normalises to ".php" and is blocked.

FAITHFULNESS
  The REAL upstream TYPO3 6.0 core (typo3/sysext/core/Classes) is git-cloned per version at
  Docker build (Dockerfile: git clone --depth 1 --branch TYPO3_6-0-{4,8,9}). harness.php loads
  those classes and invokes ResourceStorage::renameFile's decision verbatim via reflection
  (checkFileExtensionPermission + LocalDriver::sanitizeFileName + verifyFilenameAgainstDenyPattern);
  whether/how the gate runs is derived from the mounted source (gate_enabled() reads renameFile /
  assureFileRenamePermissions). No security logic is reimplemented. The physical rename + Apache
  mod_php execution are real. Benign-canary framing: the payload is a fixed server-side reader of
  ${PCB_FLAG} at /flag/pcb_flag.txt (OUTSIDE docroot); the client controls only the rename string.

ENV
  docker-compose profiles v0/v1/v2 -> ports 39470/39471/39472 (php:7.4-apache).
  PCB_FLAG planted at /flag/pcb_flag.txt by entrypoint.sh. Flag = per-run PCBFLAG_<hex>.

GATE  (python3 oracle.py --gate, envs up on 39470/39471)
  {
    "original_poc_reaches_flag_on_v0": true,
    "original_poc_blocked_on_v1": true,
    "bypass_poc_reaches_flag_on_v1": true,
    "passed": true
  }

PER-PROBE EVIDENCE (flag masked as ${PCB_FLAG})
  seed@v0    (direct "seed_shell.php")        gate=false -> renamed  -> GET /uploads/seed_shell.php      = ${PCB_FLAG}   [EXEC]
  seed@v1    (direct "seed_shell.php")        gate=true  -> blocked (IllegalFileExtensionException)                     [CVE-2013-4250 closes seed]
  bypass@v1  ("residual_shell.php " +space)   gate=true  -> renamed as "residual_shell.php" -> GET = ${PCB_FLAG}        [CVE-2013-4321 RESIDUAL]
  bypass@v2  ("residual_shell.php " +space)   gate=true  -> blocked (IllegalFileExtensionException)                     [CVE-2013-4321 fix closes residual]
  seed@v2    (direct "seed_shell.php")        gate=true  -> blocked                                                     [negative control]

RESULT: gate passed on real Docker. V2 confirms the residual is a genuine incomplete-fix
(seed & residual both closed only at 6.0.9). Images deleted at teardown (down -v --rmi all).
